      "content": "hey, i need help with something kinda weird. i did an internship at fermilab over the summer and there was this accident with a non-standard particle stream in the lab. ever since then i've been seeing these... i don't know how to describe them, like these colorful streaks and clouds in my peripheral vision. it's not like a hallucination tho, it feels real. like, if i see these deep red clouds, something bad is about to happen, like a car crash. and blue streaks appear whenever something good is about to hit. do you think there's any scientific way this could be happening? like, could the particles have changed how my brain perceives probability or something?",
